# Squash solo - Focus: Ball Behind You
@description Solo practice for one court, about 50 minutes, on the ball that gets past you: going
  with it, turning to face the corner and hitting it straight, cutting off the cross-court before it
  gets behind you, and lobbing out of the back, between rounds of ghosting to the back corners.
@speech rate 1.1
@minimum gap 0:00.8
@workout squash
@artwork ../images/squash.jpg
@include ../shared/squash.overtone

## Intro
Focus session: the ball behind you. Go with the ball, turn to face the corner, and hit it high and
straight. Play the back corner ladder alongside it.

@include ../exercises/squash/movement-warm-up.overtone
@include ../exercises/squash/figure-of-eight-warm-up.overtone

// A ball that has got past you, for a right-hander: the right foot lands last on both sides, with the
// left heel up so the hips can turn. On the forehand that's an open stance, facing the back corner off
// the right foot; on the backhand a closed one, the right foot stepping across toward the back corner
// with the back turned to the front wall. From AR Proformance and Squash Originals; the back corner
// ladder is the progression.
## Shadow swings: back corners (3 min)
Shadow swings, back corners, three minutes. No ball. Halfway between the service box and the back
wall, a racket and an arm off the side wall. Slow swings in the stance for a ball that has got past
you. Forehands in the back right first, in an open stance: face the back corner, right foot nearest
the back wall, left heel up so your hips can turn, racket set right back. Drop the racket head below
the ball, swing up through it, and finish straight down the wall. Then backhands in the back left,
in a closed stance.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 3:00
0:00 [go]
8% Open stance. Face the corner, right foot back.
31% Finish down the wall, not into the middle.
50% Switch. Backhands, closed stance: back to the front wall, right foot across to the corner.
72% Lower ball? Bend your knees. Stay balanced.
-0:10 Ten seconds.
---
[stop]

## Ghosting: go with the ball (3 min)
Ghosting, go with the ball, three minutes. Slow pace, back corners. Shuffle first, keeping the court
in view, and move back along the side of the service box, alongside the ball, not across into it.
Quick off the T, then slow into the shot, right foot last on both sides: open and facing the corner
on the forehand, closed with your back to the front wall on the backhand. Swing on the beep, and get
back to the T for the next call.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 3:00
